      "filename": "1973 AMC Hornet X with Levis option at AMO 2015 meet-1of4.jpg",
      "title": "File:1973 AMC Hornet X with Levis option at AMO 2015 meet-1of4.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/1973_AMC_Hornet_X_with_Levis_option_at_AMO_2015_meet-1of4.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1973_AMC_Hornet_X_with_Levis_option_at_AMO_2015_meet-1of4.jpg",
      "width": 3264,
      "height": 2448,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "CZmarlin  — Christopher Ziemnowicz, a photo credit is requested if this image is used anywhere other than Wikipedia, and please also leave a note at Wikipedia here. Thank you!",
      "description": "1973 AMC Hornet X, a sporty compact-sized hatchback made by American Motors Corporation. This Pewter Silver (paint code E5) car has the optional Levis interior. Real denim was not used because it was not tough enough to serve as automobile upholstery. AMC turned to spun nylon that looked like the genuine article, as well as copper Levis rivets, traditional contrasting stitching, and even the Levi’s tab on both the front seat backs. The option also included unique door panels with Levis trim and removable map pockets, as well as Levis decals on the front fenders. The X package included coordinated \"rally\" side stripes, 14 x 6-inch slot-style steel wheels with C78 x 14 Polyglas blackball tires, an \"X\" emblem, and a sports steering wheel. Picture taken at the American Motors Owners Association (AMO) annual convention that was held July 2015 near Cleveland, Ohio.",
      "dateCreated": "2015-07-25 12:03:30",
