      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "CZmarlin — Christopher Ziemnowicz, a photo credit would be appreciated if this image is used anywhere other than Wikipedia.",
      "description": "1973 AMC Gremlin X with the Levi’s interior trim option finished in Maxi Blue with white stripes. A sporty subcompact car built by American Motors Corporation (AMC). The optional interior features spun nylon that looked like demin, as well as copper Levis rivets, traditional contrasting stitching, and even the Levi’s tab on both the front seat backs. The option also included unique door panels with Levis trim and removable map pockets, as well as Levis decals on the front fenders.  The X package includes: slot-style 14x6-inch road wheels, D70x14 white letter tires, sport steering wheel, custom interior package with bucket seats, interior appointment package, cargo area insulation and carpet, as well as body side stripes, rear panel, and body painted grille with accent stripe. Photographs were taken during the 2017 American Motors Owners (AMO) convention that was held in Gettysburg, Pennsylvania. This show was organized by the Potomac Ramblers Automobile Club.",
      "dateCreated": "2017-06-24 12:08:49",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "levi-strauss-co-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "9q8z",
